# Response headers for Cloudflare Workers static assets.
#
# Astro copies public/ into dist/ verbatim, so this file ships with the build.
# Cloudflare's default for every asset is `public, max-age=0, must-revalidate`,
# which is right for HTML — a docs edit should be live immediately — and wrong
# for fingerprinted assets, which can be cached forever.
#
# Patterns allow one splat per rule, anywhere in it, and it matches across
# slashes: `/*.webp` is every WebP at any depth. A one-segment wildcard is
# spelled `:name`. The `.md` twins need no rule: Wrangler types them from the
# extension, and they keep the HTML pages' `max-age=0` on purpose.
#
# Paths here are the *built* paths, never prefixed with `site.basePath`, even on
# a site served under a subpath. The Worker strips that prefix before it calls
# `ASSETS.fetch()` (see `assetRequest` in worker/index.ts), so matching happens
# against the already-stripped path — the same shape as `dist/`.
#
# Getting this wrong fails in the worst available way rather than loudly. A
# `/docs/_astro/*` rule on a `/docs` site matches nothing and falls through to
# Cloudflare's `max-age=0, must-revalidate` default, so every fingerprinted
# asset is revalidated on every page view — while the `/*` block below still
# applies and makes the file look like it is working. A test enforces it: see
# test/components.test.mjs, 'every _headers rule matches something the build
# produced'.

/*
  # A year, without includeSubDomains or preload: this is a shared workers.dev
  # hostname, and either of those would impose the policy on sibling projects.
  # A custom domain should add both.
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), geolocation=(), microphone=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin

# Media, matched by extension so the rule follows the file wherever it lives:
# `/screenshots/`, the share cards in `/og/`, the language marks in `/icons/`,
# or a folder beside the page that shows it, which is where content migrated
# from Mintlify, Docusaurus or Starlight keeps its images. A rule per folder
# covers only the folders someone remembered to list; one site served 2,344
# images from page folders at Cloudflare's `max-age=0` default, so every one of
# them was revalidated on every view.
#
# None of these names is content-addressed: replacing a screenshot keeps its
# name. So a day of freshness and a week of grace, never `immutable`, which
# keeps a replaced image from staying wrong for long. SVG here is the favicon,
# diagrams and icons, which change on a framework upgrade at most.
#
# These come before every more specific rule on purpose. Rules are applied in
# file order and their headers combine, so a second `Cache-Control` would be
# appended rather than replace this one. A later rule that needs a different
# value removes this one first with `! Cache-Control`, as `/_astro/*` does.
#
# `wrangler.jsonc` excludes the same extensions from `run_worker_first`, so none
# of these costs a Worker invocation. A test keeps the two lists in step.
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/*.avif
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/*.jpeg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/*.gif
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/*.mp4
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/*.webm
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/*.svg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800, stale-while-revalidate=604800

# Content-addressed: the filename changes whenever the bytes do, so a repeat
# visitor never revalidates the CSS, the JS bundle or the self-hosted fonts.
# `! Cache-Control` first: an image imported into a page lands here too, and
# would otherwise carry the media rule's value appended to this one.
/_astro/*
  ! Cache-Control
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable

# Fetched once per session, on the first search. Short freshness window plus a
# long grace period, so it is effectively instant without going stale for long.
/search-index.json
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, stale-while-revalidate=604800

